From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Faye-Lund <erik.faye-lund@arm.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:56:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: plug precomp-shader leak

We need to free the struct panfrost_precomp_shader that we allocated in
panfrost_precomp_shader_create(), otherwise we leak memory here. It's
not a lot, but let's clean it up nevertheless.

Fixes: 8adede1d44e8 ("panfrost: Implement precomp dispatch on Gallium")
Reviewed-by: Boris Brezillon <boris.brezillon@collabora.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8b07f64a383f19c7002a4e97f422bbd01e9d4f54)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit 7898743c038215e41d3598c411e7bf9a57927756)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_precomp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_precomp.c b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_precomp.c
index c9b0c9b62fe..ea2f2c49893 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_precomp.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_precomp.c
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ static void
 panfrost_precomp_shader_destroy(struct panfrost_precomp_cache *cache,
                                 struct panfrost_precomp_shader *shader)
 {
-   /* XXX: Do we have anything to do here? */
+   FREE(shader);
 }
 
 void
